===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂el- (other)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|all}}, from {{inh|en|ang|eall}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*all}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*allaz}}, of uncertain origin<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref> but perhaps from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂el-|t=beyond, other}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|al||all}}, {{cog|nl|al||all}}, {{cog|sco|a'||all}}, {{cog|de|all||all}}, {{cog|sv|all||all}}, {{cog|no|all||all}}, {{cog|is|allur||all}}, {{cog|cy|holl||all}}, {{cog|ga|uile||all}}, {{cog|lt|aliái||all, each, every}}.

The dialectal sense “all gone” is a {{cal|en|de|alle|nocap=1}}. The use in {{m|en||who all, where all}} etc. also has equivalents in German (see {{m|de|alles}}).

