==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|al}}, from {{inh|de|goh|al}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*all}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*allaz}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|all}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/al/}}
* {{audio|de|De-all.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-all2.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|al|s=1}}

===Determiner===
{{head|de|determiner}}

# [[#English|all]]
#: {{ux|de|'''Alle''' Menschen sind gleich.|'''All''' people are equal.}}
#: {{ux|de|Du musst doch nicht '''allen''' Unsinn nachmachen, den du hörst!|You needn't reproduce '''all''' nonsense that you hear!}}
#* '''1843''', Karl Ludwig Kannegießer (translation from Italian into German), ''Die göttliche Komödie des Dante Alighieri'', 4th edition, 1st part, Leipzig, p. 84:
#*: {{quote|de|... / Nachdem, von Wuth und Grausamkeit entbronnen, / Der Weiberschwarm die Männer '''all''' erschlug.}}
# [[every]] {{gloss|in time intervals, with plural noun}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir treffen uns '''alle''' zwei Wochen.|We meet up '''every''' two weeks.}}

====Usage notes====
* The bare form '''{{m|de||all}}''' is used with articles and pronouns, which it precedes (as in English). For instance: {{m|de||all die Sachen|all the things}}; {{m|de||all dies[es] Gerede|all this chitchat}}; {{m|de||all[e] meine Freunde|all my friends}} {{q|more common with the e}}. Colloquial German often uses the adjective {{m|de|ganz}} instead: {{m|de||die ganzen Sachen; dies[es] ganze Gerede; meine ganzen Freunde}}.
* If '''{{m|de||all}}''' is followed by an adjective, the adjective is declined weakly: {{m|de||alle guten Sachen|all good things}}, {{m|de||alles Gute|all the best}}

